{{HERE IS THE CLAIM: }}

{{I represent my client, Masis Avedisian (email address: masis.avendisian18@gmail.com), in the current case regarding an alleged parking violation linked to his Bolt account. After reviewing the material provided to my client, it has emerged that there is a significant deficiency in your evidence. The ID number provided in your written communication does not match the ID number shown in the attached image of the evidence. This discrepancy creates significant doubt about the accuracy of the evidence and thus the legal basis for the issued charge.}}

According to Chapter 2, Section 1 of the Constitution, every individual has the right to protection against unjustified interference by the public, and even if you are a private company, measures that may have legal and financial consequences must rest on a correct and reliable basis. Furthermore, the Contracts Act (1915:218) states that parties to a contract shall act in good faith and faithfully fulfill their obligations. Incorrect or contradictory documentation cannot be considered to meet this requirement. In light of the above, I demand that you immediately write off the current fee until you can present coherent and correct evidence that unequivocally supports your claim. Should this not happen, my client reserves the right to refer the matter to the Swedish General Complaints Board (ARN) and, if necessary, to the competent court for review.

I hereby dispute the additional fee of 630 SEK for scooter 432957 on July 16, 2025, as the parking was approved according to your own app and parking function. At the time, the designated parking space was full, but the app nonetheless approved that I park in the location where the scooter was left, which clearly shows that the responsibility for this error lies with Bolt and not with me as the user.

I would also like to point out that, according to the attached images, other customers have parked in the same way, which makes this fee appear unfair and discriminatory. This handling therefore feels unfounded and unjustified.My scooter with ID 432957 was parked in a location that, according to your app, was approved, despite the area being full. However, in the attached evidence photo, ID 529-809 is shown, which does not correspond to my scooter. This indicates an error in the documentation and warrants a reconsideration of the fee.

