As you may be aware, the right of access under data protection law does not provide an individual with an absolute right of full access to any and all documents containing their personal data. For example, that right should not adversely affect the rights of others. Furthermore, we must point out that if after careful analysis we conclude that our rights or rights of others prevail, we will not be able to provide you with access to certain documentation where such an exemption applies. 



Consequently, please note that we are not allowed to share the personal data concerning third parties as the GDPR requires us to respect the rights and freedoms of other data subjects when satisfying the right of access requests.



